# WT: the image path in the real app against the fake server, as alexk in Couch Co-op's #general.
# Two PNGs sent as one message, drawn at the box their attachment measures; the list fetches each
# image's file; one opens in the viewer at full size.
#
# The fake server reports every attachment with hasThumbnail false and no width or height
# (crates/semaphore-fake-server/src/messages.rs, `add_attachment`), so the list asks for
# /file/{id} and never /thumbnail, and every box is the 320 x 200 a server with no measurement
# gets. The box shapes the server would give it are the stories' (rigs/shot/scripts/wt-thumbnails.steps);
# what this proves is the fetch and the viewer, and that the thumbnail branch is not taken when the
# server says there is no thumbnail.

app 1280 800
wait idle
click auth-connect
wait core label "Username" within 5
click auth-username
type "alexk"
click auth-password
type "hunter2"
click auth-login
wait core session signed-in
wait core connection connected
wait core channel $ID(cc-general)
wait core rows >= 14
wait core file-ready sc-img-pit within 10
wait idle

# 1. Two images in one message: uploaded, attached, and drawn.
attach rigs/slice/fixtures/sketch.png
attach rigs/slice/fixtures/sketch.png
type "two pictures"
press enter
wait core sent "two pictures"
wait core attachments "two pictures" 2 within 15
wait core uploads "two pictures" 0
wait core pending-files "two pictures" 0
expect requests FileUploadController_uploadFile >= 2
expect requests MessagesController_addAttachment >= 2
# The fake server seeds the scenario's soundboard files (four communities, three sounds each)
# and numbers uploads from there: one message's first two are the 13th and 14th.
wait core file-ready 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000d within 15
wait core file-ready 0000f11e-0000-4000-8000-00000000000e within 15
wait idle
shot 01-uploaded

# 2. The list fetched each image at full size, and asked for no thumbnail.
expect requests FileController_getFile >= 2
expect core requests FileController_getFileThumbnail == 0

# 3. The viewer, at full size; Escape closes it.
click-row image "two pictures" 0
wait core viewer open
wait idle
shot 02-viewer
press escape
wait core viewer closed
